  "THE_DECISIVE_NUMBER": "at the mandated n = 50 the locked daughter endpoint has 1.65 % power against F_INTEGRATED, against the 80.15 % the handoff computed for the saturated endpoint.",
  "WHY_NO_LARGER_n_FIXES_IT": "1/256 = 0.0039 is 1.22x the floor F_INTEGRATED = 0.0032. The alternative sits essentially on the null, so power rises only marginally with n; at n = 2000 it is still under 10 %. This is not a sample-size shortfall, it is an endpoint at the floor.",
  "WHAT_THIS_DOES_NOT_MEAN": "it does not mean the daughter fails to persist. The daughter interval survives a median of 230 steps after the removal, up to 1472. What it means is that the BINARY frozen COMPLETE_TURNOVER, restricted to that one identity, is expressed in 1 of 22 worlds, because the strict identity rule terminates on SPLIT_OR_TIE in all 22 before a second turnover completes inside the interval.",
